// Your monitor / output configuration. niri only auto-arranges if you
// leave this empty — most setups want explicit positions, scales, and
// modes.
//
// Discover your outputs: `niri msg outputs`
// Wiki:                  https://niri-wm.github.io/niri/Configuration:-Outputs
//
// Example (laptop + external):
//
//     output "eDP-1" {
//         mode "2880x1800@60"
//         scale 1.5
//         position x=0 y=0
//     }
//     output "DP-1" {
//         mode "2560x1440@144"
//         scale 1
//         position x=1920 y=0
//         variable-refresh-rate
//     }
//
// Portrait monitor: `transform "90"` (CCW) or `"270"` (CW). On a
// portrait screen you may also want a per-output `layout { … }` so
// new columns open wider than the default 50 %.
